course: dictionary
lesson: 5482
title: A lateen sail
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A new word often shows its meaning in the sentence around it. Read this: «The Portuguese and Spanish used caravels, small fast ships with triangular lateen sails that could sail closer to the wind.»
explain: Triangular tells you the sail has three corners, and sails are the cloth that catches the wind. So a lateen sail is a three-cornered sail on a ship.
explain: The sentence also tells you that a lateen sail helps a ship sail closer to the wind. Check your idea by putting it in the sentence in place of the hard word. If it still makes sense, you are probably right.
fact: A lateen sail is a triangular sail tied to a long pole that hangs at an angle on a short mast.
fact: A lateen-rigged boat is a boat with a lateen sail.
fact: Lateen can be a noun too: a lateen is a boat with such a sail.
fact: In history lessons, lateen sails helped dhows and caravels sail closer to the wind, which made long sea journeys possible.
exercise: «The Portuguese and Spanish used caravels, small fast ships with triangular lateen sails.» What shape is a lateen sail? | Square like a window | Long and flat like a ribbon | *Triangular | Round
exercise: What is a lateen sail tied to? | *A long pole that hangs at an angle | A wooden wheel | A rope tied to the anchor | A short mast only
exercise: Why did lateen sails help caravels on long journeys? | *They let ships sail closer to the wind | They made the boats sink | They made the boats heavier | They stopped the wind blowing
test: Which of these is a lateen? | A flag on a castle | A type of fish | A tall tower on the shore | *A boat with a lateen sail
test: Which word describes a boat with this kind of sail? | triangle | *lateen-rigged | sailcloth | mast-free
exam: Which best explains what a lateen sail is? | A tall tower on a ship | A round sail with many ropes | *A triangular sail tied to a long pole that hangs at an angle | A flag on the top of a castle
